mentum cluster carries ~44% of weight — acceptable given the current trending/dispersion regime; monitor for convergence.\n- **High turnover**: vix_beta (3.35), vol_adj_mom (3.15), downside_vol (3.16) have turnover_10d_rank > 3 — with 3 bps one-way friction and a 10-day horizon, these are near the cost ceiling; do not increase further.\n- **Regime-specific**: beta_ew (dir +1) conflicts with the current risk-off tape — kept at 0.03 as a tactical residual only. VIX spike could mean-revert; if VIX falls back below 17, revisit vix_beta weight.\n\n## Trading Feedback\n- `memory.txt` is empty (0 bytes) — no live PnL attribution or execution issues to incorporate this cycle. First online allocation; no factor-level performance feedback yet.\n\n## Notable Observations\n- No new miner output this cycle; library unchanged (11 effective factors, capacity 30, no evictions pending). Ensemble is a continuity of the confirmed set with a small defensive refinement (vix_beta 0.17→0.18, beta_ew 0.04→0.03, eurusd 0.07→0.06, amihud 0.03→0.04) driven by the fresh VIX spike and broad EW-basket negative drift.\n- WTI (+27% 20d, +43% 126d) and US10Y (+5.8% 63d) are the standout positive trends; crypto remains the weakest block (BTC −17.5%, ETH −14.8% at 63d). Expect the momentum block to express long WTI/yields and short crypto/CN-tech if trends persist.\n- Watch: SOX/STAR50 prints show +0.0% over 5d (stale/zero rows) — flagged in the data pipeline; they do not affect the ensemble but may impact factor coverage at the edges."
